Pymtheg patch 0013 (C-21, not upstream): `where dyn Trait: Bound`.

Accepts valid Rust: a trait object type on the left of a where predicate
(`where dyn CipherSuiteSelector: VersionSuiteSelector<T>,`). Any type may be
bounded there; this adds `dynamic_type` to the types upstream lists.
Reference: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/generics.html#where-clauses
Upstream: no issue or pull request for this shape. The open meta issue
https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/issues/229 lists rustc's
tests/ui/trivial-bounds/trivial-bounds-object.rs, whose `where dyn A + 'static: A`
(a bounded trait object on the left) this patch does not cover.

